  "headline": "The 443-row OpenPoly calibration corpus used by all four prior signed novelty audits (fingerprint-coefficient-robustness-v1, conformal-anomaly-detection-v1, cross-family-concordance-v1, mondrian-conditional-coverage-v1) contains only 350 canonically-distinct structures: 129 of 443 rows (29.1%) are exact structural duplicates across 36 alias groups (max group size 12, e.g. PNIPAM/PNIPAAm/NIPAM aliases x12, PLA/PLLA/PDLA/poly(lactic acid) aliases x6), violating the Vovk-Gammerman-Shafer exchangeability precondition every prior receipt cites. Deduplicating and recomputing the identical per-family conformal pipeline flips 5 already-signed family/alpha novelty cells for 3 candidates (DDS, IPDA, m-XDA), including the specific signed fact cross-family-concordance-v1 reports as DDS's ONLY novel-calling family (maccs_166, alpha=0.05): that cell flips from NOVEL=True to NOVEL=False, so DDS's true cross-family count is 0/4 novel at alpha=0.05, not the signed 1/4.",
  "hypothesis_evaluation": {
    "h0": "The 443-row OpenPoly calibration corpus is exchangeable (443 distinct structures); prior signed per-family/per-alpha novelty verdicts are invariant to deduplication.",
    "interpretation": "The calibration corpus is not exchangeable: 129/443 rows are re-listings of 36 already-present structures under different literature names. This is not a cosmetic issue -- deduplicating and rerunning the IDENTICAL signed pipeline changes already-signed alpha-threshold verdicts, including the one fact cross-family-concordance-v1 reports as DDS's sole novel-calling family. The core Morgan(r2,2048) family used by the original fixed-0.40 and primary conformal-anomaly-detection-v1 claims does NOT flip for any of the 5 candidates at any alpha in this check (drift_morgan_r2_2048 shows p moving 12-39% but no threshold crossing) -- so the headline 5/5-fixed-cut and morgan-family conformal verdicts survive. The cross-family UNANIMITY accounting does not: it is measurably wrong about which specific families call DDS novel.",
    "verdict": "H0_REFUTED__CORPUS_CONTAINS_DUPLICATE_STRUCTURES__PRIOR_SIGNED_VERDICTS_FLIP"
  },
  "method": "Group corpus rows by canonical RDKit SMILES of the wildcard-capped PSMILES ('*'->'C'). For contaminated (n=443, as-signed) and deduped (n=350, first literature row per unique structure) corpora, recompute per family in {morgan_r2_2048, maccs_166, atompair_2048, toptorsion_2048}: LOO nonconformity alpha_i=1-NN_LOO(i); candidate alpha_x=1-max_j Tanimoto(x,corpus_j); smoothed-free conformal p=(#{alpha_i>=alpha_x}+1)/(n+1); NOVEL iff p<alpha for alpha in {0.01,0.05,0.10,0.20}. Report per family/alpha/candidate flips between contaminated and deduped verdicts.",
  "n_flip_cells": 5,
  "non_circularity": "Dedup key is canonical RDKit SMILES only (Chem.MolToSmiles), computed without reading Tg, Name semantics, or any novelty/alpha field, so it cannot import the answer. Corpus is the identical SHA-256-locked read-only OpenPoly CSV all four prior receipts use. The Morgan(r2,2048) lane on the untouched 443-row corpus must reproduce the independently-signed per-candidate NN Tanimoto to <1e-12 before any dedup-drift claim is trusted.",
  "purpose": "Test the untested exchangeability precondition of the shared corpus-construction code inherited unmodified by all four prior amphora-molecule-novelty audit receipts: are the 443 calibration rows 443 distinct structures (as conformal validity requires) or a smaller set of unique structures replicated under literature aliases?",
